at 5:29PM MDT until October 25 at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding likely along the Rio Grande between Monte Vista and\nAlamosa.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Rio Grande County and West Central Alamosa\nCounty...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 PM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the Rio Grande and low lying agricultural\nareas in Rio Grande and Alamosa counties is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 525 PM MDT, Emergency management reports flooding of low lying\nareas along and near the Rio Grande in Rio Grande county and in\nAlamosa county upstream of the city of Alamosa.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande and West Central\nAlamosa Counties between Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dec66dcc50c62eb3136a29e188c17eb9595591f1.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dec66dcc50c62eb3136a29e188c17eb9595591f1.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 24 at 1:55PM MDT until October 26 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...Forecast flooding changed to Minor severity and increased in\nduration for the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande Near Del Norte affecting Rio Grande County.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Del Norte, Alamosa...Minor\nflooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...Until Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 5.5 feet, Minor Flood. The Del Norte Riverwalk Trail\nfloods.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 12:45 PM MDT Saturday the stage was 5.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 5.5 feet\ntomorrow morning. It will then fall below flood stage tomorrow\nevening.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 5.5\nfeet on 06/18/1995.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-26T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cccc4ae9e9f411d5eef265b45b3cf8740aab11ad.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cccc4ae9e9f411d5eef265b45b3cf8740aab11ad.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T23:52:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 242352 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 552 PM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rain likely to occur over parts of the southeast plains this afternoon into tonight. - Low lying agricultural flooding in the western side of the San Luis Valley likely for the next day or two. - dry weather through next week. - Another impactful storm possi","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T17:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 241720 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1120 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-251730- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T19:49:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... Meteorological conditions for extreme fire behavior are not anticipated during this forecast period. It will be wet across the district through Sunday night as a strong Pacific trough moves over the region. The precipitation over the mountains will be more showery, while over the eastern plains (especially far eastern plains) will have heavy rain from this afternoon into Sunday nigh",